    "blocks": [
      {
        "blockId": "syntax-concept",
        "dimensions": [
          "syntax",
          "concept"
        ],
        "text": "Review activities作主语，account for连接most of the remaining work；most of给出的是比例性概括，不是原因从句。 分母是remaining work，不是整个项目，也不是已经完成的工作。句子没有给出具体百分比或工作量单位。",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "cambridge-account-for",
            "sourceVersion": "2026-11-16",
            "locator": "Business English, part of a total",
            "supportedClaim": "account for可表示占总体的一部分，不等于说明原因。",
            "url": "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account-for?topic=existing-and-being"
          }
        ],
        "title": "句子结构与当前所指"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "contrast",
        "dimensions": [
          "contrast"
        ],
        "text": "account for a discrepancy通常是解释差异；account for most of a total是构成大部分。看到数量、比例或总体时要检查是否采用构成义。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "容易混淆的地方"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "game-neighbors",
        "dimensions": [
          "languageGame",
          "englishNeighbors"
        ],
        "text": "这是工作量构成说明。接下来可问剩余工作如何计量、评审包含哪些任务，从而安排资源，而不是立刻寻找谁造成问题。 account for X percent与share/proportion相连；remaining work则限定总体范围，讨论总工作量时不可省略。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "讨论通常怎样继续"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "action",
        "dimensions": [
          "pragmaticAction"
        ],
        "text": "说话者在突出剩余工作中评审所占的比重，为关注评审资源提供理由。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "说话者正在做什么"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "workplace",
        "dimensions": [
          "workplaceUse"
        ],
        "text": "下面是迁移到制造业沟通的新例句；不代表原场景中已发生的决定。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "迁移到工作情境"
      }
    ],
    "workplaceUse": [
      {
